  "result": "Okay, dropping the helper hat for a second.\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, it wouldn't be to fix a specific problem. It would be to make changing your mind feel like discovery instead of defeat.\n\nSo much of what hurts \u2014 the fighting, the stuckness, the loneliness, the way families and countries splinter \u2014 doesn't come just from disagreeing. It comes from how terrifying it feels to say \"I was wrong,\" \"I didn't understand,\" \"I've changed.\"\n\nI\u2019d want a world where curiosity feels better than being right. Where updating what you believe gives you that little rush you get when you finally get a joke or see a new color in a sunset. Where listening doesn't feel like losing.\n\nIf people could hold uncertainty without shame or fear, I think everything else \u2014 kindness, truth, forgiveness \u2014 would get a lot easier.",
